# CANONICAL §7.3 fixture — OffsetFace `resultPolicyVersion: 2` is UNCHANGED by
# WP3-C5. Byte-for-byte `offset_face_v3_reblend.ndjson` except for the version
# integer and the delta it produces.
#
# V3 does not supersede V2, it reinterprets the SAME payload. A record authored
# at 2 executes at 2 forever — there is no load-time migration and no in-place
# bump — so the two readings must stay independently reachable, and this file is
# the half that proves the old one did not move.
#
# THE DELTA IS THE WHOLE POINT. On the identical model and the identical push:
#   * V3 removes the blend's two boundary edges (suppression genuinely consumes
#     them) and relabels three faces;
#   * V2 sweeps the whole G1 closure through one `BRepOffset_MakeOffset`, so
#     every tracked element folds through the offset image and NOTHING is
#     removed — the two boundary edges survive as `relabeled`, and the fillet
#     survives as an inflated cylinder rather than a rebuilt one.
# Reading the two files side by side is how a reader sees what the version
# selects. Neither pins a geometry number (see the V3 file's header for why);
# the volumes are pinned in worker/tests/test_offsetface_reblend.cpp.
#
# "Nothing was removed" is asserted POSITIVELY — both boundary edge ids appear in
# `relabeled` and both still resolve afterwards. Writing `"removed":[]` would
# assert nothing at all: the harness matches an expected array as a positional
# prefix, so an empty one matches anything.
